{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vt6rSbiUukfknGMuZSUwdH","type":"tool_result","content":"439\t    holds throughout.\n440\t    \"\"\"\n441\t    message = git_out(root, [\"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%B\", rev]) or \"\"\n442\t    lines = message.splitlines()\n443\t    subject = lines[0].strip() if lines else \"\"\n444\t    parent = _rev(root, rev + \"^1\")\n445\t    if parent is None or _rev(root, rev + \"^2\") is not None:\n446\t        return None\n447\t    listing = git_bytes(\n448\t        root, [\"diff\", \"--name-status\", \"--no-renames\", \"-z\", parent, rev]\n449\t    )\n450\t    if listing is None:\n451\t        return None\n452\t    fields = [field for field in listing.split(b\"\\0\") if field]\n453\t    wi_ids = _closed_wi_ids(fields)\n454\t    if wi_ids is None or subject != mechanical_close_subject(wi_ids):\n455\t        return None\n456\t    return parent\n457\t\n458\t\n459\tdef _peel_target(root, branch, rev):\n460\t    \"\"\"The rev a DISPOSABLE commit at `rev` peels to, or None when `rev` is not\n461\t    one. TWO commits are disposable and this is their one home, so\n462\t    `governing_rev`'s walk asks the question once: the station's REFRESH (which\n463\t    re-merges trunk and regenerates) and the machinery's own ADJUDICATION CLOSE\n464\t    (which archives a judged row terminal). Both are machine-authored, both move\n465\t    the tree without the lane having changed what it is claiming, and both are\n466\t    admitted by verification against git rather than by measurement.\"\"\"\n467\t    attested = refresh_attestation(root, branch, rev)\n468\t    if attested is not None:\n469\t        return attested[0]\n470\t    return mechanical_close_attestation(root, rev)\n471\t\n472\t\n473\tdef work_tip(root, branch):\n474\t    \"\"\"The branch's last WORK commit as a sha: the tip, with any refresh commit\n475\t    peeled off at the work sha that refresh ITSELF recorded.\n476\t\n477\t    Two callers, one meaning. `integrate.refresh` resets here before it merges\n478\t    (the §A2.1 disposable-commit rule: a retry never stacks a second merge on\n479\t    the first, because docs/log.md is append-compiled and the stack would\n480\t    conflict on the file end). `governing_identity` measures code-time here,\n481\t    because the refresh is MECHANICAL bookkeeping - it rewrites the compiled log\n482\t    and the generated artifacts, and if that counted as code it would stale the\n483\t    honest APPROVE that had to precede it.\n484\t\n485\t    The peel is why `refresh_attestation` had to become a verification rather\n486\t    than a substring test: this function feeds a `reset --hard`, so peeling one\n487\t    commit too far DESTROYS committed work. A work commit whose message merely\n488\t    quoted the trailer used to be peeled, and its file left the branch (REVIEW-A\n489\t    round 1, driven). Now nothing is peeled that does not carry its own tree and\n490\t    parent, which an ordinary commit cannot do by accident.\n491\t    \"\"\"\n492\t    rev = branch\n493\t    for _ in range(_MAX_REFRESH_PEEL):\n494\t        attested = refresh_attestation(root, branch, rev)\n495\t        if attested is None:\n496\t            return _rev(root, rev)\n497\t        rev = attested[0]\n498\t    return _rev(root, rev)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9fc475e-d3d6-4b26-9e61-40a41045c15b","uuid":"93befe7b-5ccc-4481-aaf4-7ae1aaa0cc18","timestamp":"2026-09-05T02:07:55.699Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-595-llr-207-tc-205-return-and-llr/project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py","content":"    holds throughout.\n    \"\"\"\n    message = git_out(root, [\"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%B\", rev]) or \"\"\n    lines = message.splitlines()\n    subject = lines[0].strip() if lines else \"\"\n    parent = _rev(root, rev + \"^1\")\n    if parent is None or _rev(root, rev + \"^2\") is not None:\n        return None\n    listing =