ndow, and a back-to-back paired run gave BASE 56.83s vs TIP 57.22s — my delta is ~0.4s. Cause was two other sessions' `-n auto` suites on a 6-CPU box. All four readings are in the log fragment.\n\n**I killed my first full-suite run and re-ran it.** Two commits and a `git checkout` probe landed in the working tree while it was running, so its result described no single tree. The reported `1 failed, 3394 passed, 21 skipped in 1026.12s` is the clean re-run; the one red is the known `docs/stage` fingerprint node, driven both ways again (green at the base; green at this tip on a regenerated-stage worktree where every other derived field, `drafted = 11` included, is byte-identical).\n\n**Surfaced, not fixed:** no spine row's `code_symbol` names `station.py`'s mechanical-close vocabulary (`MECHANICAL_CLOSE_PREFIX/SUFFIX`, `mechanical_close_subject`, and now `mechanical_close_order`). That gap predates this lane; closing it is an `LLR-182` amendment and isn't this row's to take.\n\nNo `Status` was flipped anywhere in the branch delta and no `docs/archive/last_approved/` written — the approval act stays the adjudicator's."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":184796,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":237},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9fc475e-d3d6-4b26-9e61-40a41045c15b","uuid":"417d39b8-a7d0-4137-ba43-27a5340182f1","request_id":"req_011CejZLwSXfPfVmmJqDBLQb"}
